# Local AI-assistant workspace: per-machine settings, the development
# workflow skills, and scratch worktrees. Deliberately untracked — the
# repository's own design record lives in docs/agents/ and docs/code-map/,
# which ARE tracked and are what a coding agent should read.
.claude/

# Cycle session state (deleted when a change cycle completes)
/CYCLE.md

# Rust build output
target/

# Local CI mirror artifacts (make verify)
/out.pdf
/stderr.txt
/engine/lcov.info

# Full gate logs written by `make quiet T=<target>`
/.make-logs/

# Release artifacts built by `make capi-dist` / `make cli-dist` (the cdylib
# and CLI platform matrices + their checksums). Built on demand and published
# from a release run, never
# committed — a binary in the tree is a binary nobody can review.
/dist/

# SDK build/gate artifacts. Coverage reports and built gems/wheels are outputs
# of `make sdk-ruby` / `make sdk-python`, and a lockfile in a LIBRARY pins its
# consumers' resolution — a library resolves against the application's
# environment, not its own.
sdk/*/coverage/
sdk/*/*.gem
sdk/ruby/Gemfile.lock
sdk/*/dist/
sdk/*/.coverage
sdk/go/cover.out
sdk/*/htmlcov/
sdk/*/*.egg-info/
__pycache__/
.pytest_cache/
.mypy_cache/
.ruff_cache/

# A pnpm run with no global store configured writes one here.
/.pnpm-store/

# Fuzzing (`make fuzz`). The committed corpus under engine/fuzz/corpus is
# curated by hand and stays; everything a run PRODUCES is local:
#   - `generated-` seeds embed a freshly generated certificate, and the
#     signing track forbids committed key material,
#   - artifacts/ holds crash reproducers (turn one into a corpus file, with
#     a test, rather than committing the artifact); the WORKING corpus is not
#     here at all — it lives in the shojiku-fuzz-corpus named volume, because
#     libFuzzer's per-input writes are punishingly slow on a bind mount,
#   - the lockfile is fuzz-only: the crate is outside the workspace, so
#     `cargo deny` never reads it and pinning it would only add churn.
/engine/fuzz/corpus/**/generated-*
/engine/fuzz/artifacts/
/engine/fuzz/coverage/
/engine/fuzz/Cargo.lock

# .NET and Maven build outputs. Both toolchains write into the package tree the
# gate mounts, so a gate run would otherwise dirty the working copy — the same
# reason sdk/ruby's coverage/ and sdk/python's caches are ignored above.
sdk/dotnet/**/bin/
sdk/dotnet/**/obj/
sdk/dotnet/**/TestResults/
sdk/dotnet/**/coverage.info
sdk/java/target/

# PHP gate outputs, for the same reason: phpunit writes its clover report and
# its cache into the package tree the gate mounts, and php-cs-fixer writes
# one beside them. `composer.lock` is absent from this list because there is
# nothing to lock — the package declares no dependencies at all, and the gate
# toolchain is pinned in the image.
sdk/php/build/
sdk/php/.phpunit.cache/
sdk/php/.php-cs-fixer.cache
sdk/php/vendor/
